That nostalgia extends to the clothing brand itself. &#x201C;My introduction to Tommy was when Aaliyah was rocking Tommy ,&#x201D; JoJo says, shouting out the late singer and 90s fashion star. &#x201C;Being preppy but also streetwear is something that really resonates with me because I love to inhabit that space,&#x201D; JoJo continues. &#x201C;I appreciate the classic Americana cool of it. As somebody who moved to New York three years ago, I am always looking for that wearability and that cool. It&#x2019;s no surprise that Tommy has [maintained] that cultural relevance.&#x201D;

For his part, Hilfiger says that his brand&#x2019;s integration into pop culture wasn&#x2019;t an accident; it&#x2019;s by design.&#xA0;

&#x201C;I&#x2019;ve always believed fashion is part of the conversation, but it&#x2019;s only one part of culture. You have to be curious about what people are listening to, who they&#x2019;re watching, and what they&#x2019;re excited about. That&#x2019;s where the energy comes from,&#x201D; the designer shares. &#x201C;For me, art, music, celebrity, and sport have always been connected to fashion. They&#x2019;re all ways people express who they are and what they want to be part of.&#x201D;

