JoJo and Tommy Hilfiger have both mastered the art of longevity. This year marks two decades since the release of JoJo&#x2019;s second studio album, The High Road . To celebrate, she&#x2019;ll embark on a limited seven-city acoustic run called &#x201C; The High Road: 20 Years Unplugged &#x201D; in November. She says the tour will be a &#x201C;celebration&#x201D; of the album, with most of the original tracks, as well as some beloved songs from the same era, making an appearance on the setlist.&#xA0;

It&#x2019;s the cherry on top of an exciting year for the Grammy Award-winning, multi-platinum singer, who just announced a partnership with Seeker Music . The creator-led music rights, publishing, and record company has acquired JoJo&#x2019;s original and re-recorded versions of her seminal first two albums, JoJo and The High Road , and is setting the stage for the future with special releases and projects, including a special 20th anniversary rerelease of the latter.

&#x201C;It feels really amazing because for a long time I didn&#x2019;t know what was going on with my music,&#x201D; she says of her catalog, which has been out of her own possession for years. &#x201C;Now I know what&#x2019;s going on with it, and that it&#x2019;s in good hands. People who care, who have the resources and the infrastructure to support it, to get it out there.&#x201D;

She&#x2019;s getting it out there, too. Ahead of the upcoming tour, she took the stage at Proper Presents to play an intimate acoustic set. As the singer climbed a table in the middle of the room, clad from head to toe in Tommy Hilfiger, she was surrounded by a crowd of fans who were belting The Long Way&#x2019;s biggest hit, &#x201C;Too Little Too Late&#x201D; even louder than she was, it was easy to see how JoJo&#x2019;s work&#x2014;and her stardom&#x2014;have lasted for more than two decades.&#xA0;

&#x201C;I recently worked with Cyndi Lauper on a new musical, and I asked her what she would attribute her longevity to. She said, &#x2018;You just keep going.&#x2019; That changed me,&#x201D; JoJo says. &#x201C;In life and in this industry, that&#x2019;s what it is: You just keep going.&#x201D;

JoJo was joined in Austin by Love Island USA stars Trinity Tatum and Bryce Alakai, and producer and DJ TOKiMONSTA, the latter of whom wrapped up the weekend with a set at Kappo Kappo, the Austin Proper&#x2019;s omakase sushi restaurant which was recently awarded one&#xA0;Michelin star.&#xA0;

